# Corrections log

Append-only. Never edit or delete an existing line. One line per
correction: an agent got corrected by Mike, or caught its own violation
of a rule in this system, and appends before proceeding — not after,
not "I'll log it later." `scripts/consolidate-corrections.sh` reads this
on a schedule to update `rules/DONT.md` and file promotion proposals on
repeat violations (see `DONT.md` "Promotion").

Format:
    - YYYY-MM-DD session=<id-or-name> rule=<file.md or DONT.md-row-key> what="<one line, what happened>"

`rule=` should name the file that was violated (e.g. `rule=hygiene.md`)
or, for an anti-pattern not yet promoted to its own file, the matching
`DONT.md` row's `Incident` slug (e.g. `rule=infra-into-govcon-routing`).

